Z||000000||Formula||07-28-99||11:47 AM||||I found an easy install for 2 low powered 8" subwoofer bass tubes. $160 for all the bass you'll ever need. First run your RCA wires and your remote wires  behind the passenger seat. This is easy because of the snap on console. Tuck the wires under the transmission part of the console and remove the middle console box part. Mount a small amp behind the passenger seat and connect the 2 wires.  While your console is off run the power wire to the amp. (since I have a small amp I used my cigerette lighter power supply). Take 2 16 gauge speaker wires and put them through the small hole above the cpu. Run them off to the side away from all moving parts and hot spots. I took mine around the battery. (It adds interference on the subs but you can't hear it in the cab!) Run the wires back to the trunk and connect to the tubes. (2 Jensen 375 watt bass tubes fit perfect). I put cardboard over the tubes and still have a nice size trunk. Turn on the stereo and you'll have perfect bass in the cab. (Its actually louder outside the car but your neighbors can stand a little bit). This sounds 1000X better then a free air sub in the dash. <p>The nice thing about this set up is the amp won't get as hot as it would if it was by the motor. <p>Another nice thing is you can upgrade the subs to 12" truck box style if you don't need a trunk. AND your friends can't use the cigerette lighter (WOOOOOHOOOOOOO). 
Z||000001||spike||08-03-99||07:02 AM||||My old 87 Fiero GT had 2 10 inch Pioneer Subs in a special box that I built. It covered the entire rear window. The box fit so tight that no bolts or screws were needed to hold it in place. The installation looked factory. I covered the front with matching gray vynle. Each sub was pointed at the back of the passenger & drivers head. The look and sound was perfect. I had also put a plexiglass window in the front and back of the box so I could see out the rear. I also removed the center console glove box and installed my amp in its place. The fit was perfect. I think this is the best place to install subs in a Fiero and get a custum look. Total cost to build the box was 72.00 Canadian. I will definitly build another box just like it for my next Fiero GT. Cant wait till next spring.
